<title>LITHUANIA: GOVERNMENT GUARANTEES LOAN TO BUTINGES.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT GUARANTEES LOAN TO BUTINGES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian government said on Thursday that it had approved a state guarantee for a $10 million loan to Butinges Nafta from the Union Bank of Switzerland.</p>
<p>The government's press office also said in a statement that the loan is for six months but did not give any more details.</p>
<p>The government said earlier this year that it intends to reduce its majority stake in the oil terminal project to a minority.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
